      "id": "claim_1e6a4627bacb49d486b01768ac631390",
      "statement": "pushChangesToBranch is the only post-agent git step: it runs git status --porcelain (returns success early if empty), then git add ., git commit -m <message>, and git push origin <branch>; a push failure whose stderr contains 'Permission', 'access_denied', or '403' is reported as { success: true, pushFailed: true } so the local commit is preserved and the caller decides the task outcome.",
